*---------------------- EXTENDED HEADER FIELD
* Channel `08` looks up a `#BPMxx` slot, and nothing stops a chart from pointing
* it at a value the timeline cannot use. The timing resolver skips any BPM point
* that is not finite and positive, which is the only thing keeping these charts
* from producing infinite or backwards note times:
*
*   #BPM02 0    - 240/0 is infinite seconds per measure; every later event would
*                 land at t = inf and never fire
*   #BPM03 -65  - a negative tempo runs the chart backwards
*   ZZ          - an undefined slot, which has no value at all
*
* Real players disagree on what these should do (LR2 stops or reverses the
* scroll), so the fixture pins the one thing that has to hold regardless: the
* chart still parses, and the notes before the bad change still play at the
* declared tempo.

#PLAYER 1
#LNTYPE 1

*---------------------- RESOURCES FIELD

#WAV01 sample.wav
#WAV02 branch.wav

#BPM01 130
#BPM02 0
#BPM03 -65

